# Caches, venvs and bytecode are covered by the repository root .gitignore.
# These are the artefacts this subproject generates at run time.
#
# `runs/` and `strategies/` used to be ignored wholesale, on the grounds that a
# rerun regenerates them. That is true of the caches and it is not true of these:
#
#   * `runs/research.sqlite` holds `distinct_hypotheses()`, the
#     multiple-comparisons denominator, which PLAN.md records as the one number
#     in this project that cannot be reconstructed; and
#   * it holds the sealed run, which is one-shot by construction. Re-running it
#     is not merely expensive, it is refused.
#
# So the evidence is committed and the volume is not. What stays ignored below
# is the pre-Phase-3 backup and the control-campaign databases: those *are*
# reproducible, and they are 23 MB of it.
# CSV bar caches. Git has no inline comments in .gitignore -- a trailing "#" is
# part of the pattern, so these four spent their whole life matching nothing and
# the caches were only ever untracked by luck. One pattern per line, comments
# above them.
#
#   data/        Alpaca SIP, 2016->   `aqr pull --source alpaca`
#   data-yahoo/  Yahoo, 2010->        `aqr pull --source yahoo`
#   data-deep/   Yahoo, 1995->        four bear markets
#   data-ibkr/   IBKR, 2005->         `aqr pull --source ibkr`
data/
data-yahoo/
data-deep/
data-ibkr/
runs/*.bak
runs/control-campaign*.sqlite
runs/control2/
runs/control3/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The two embargo roots are COMMITTED. They are not ignored below, and that
# is deliberate:
#
#   data-sp500/         681 series, truncated at the embargo -- the search
#   data-sp500-sealed/  682 series, full history  -- the sealed window
#
# Committing them is what makes the central claim checkable by somebody who is
# not us: `aqr seal-check` reads the files and reports that the research root
# holds no bar past 2024-09-01, and that claim is worth nothing if the files it
# reads are only on one laptop. A rebuilt cache is also not the same cache --
# Alpaca revises, and a reviewer re-pulling in 2027 would get a different tape
# and no way to tell.
#
# This does not weaken the seal. The protection was never that the sealed bars
# were hard to obtain: it is that `ResearchProvider` clamps every request at the
# embargo, that `SealedProvider` needs an explicit token *and* the sealed phase,
# and that `Bars.__post_init__` taints on sight. Those hold whether or not the
# rows are in a public repository, and the two roots stay separate directories,
# which is exactly what the audit checks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #

# Not committed: the quality-check rejects. `--keep-suspect` writes them here
# when a series fails inspection, so they are a diagnostic byproduct rather than
# either a search window or a sealed one.
data-sp500-suspect/

# NOT ignored, and it must not be: data-universes/ holds sp500_pit.json, the
# hand-reconstructed membership table with its corrections and its recorded
# non-corrections. It is source, not cache -- nothing regenerates it, and
# without it `--universe sp500_pit` does not resolve.
!data-universes/
